summary:
  Choosing an output in the box sets the one listed above it.

history:
  The first row is the system's default, so a row's number is one past its
  output's place in the list. A pick has to do what the row says.

target:
  package/contents/ui/OutputBox.qml

find:
      onActivated: (index) => chosen(OutputLogic.idAt(outs, index))

replace:
      onActivated: (index) => chosen(OutputLogic.idAt(outs, index - 1))

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_outputbox.qml::test_choosing_a_row_names_the_output_standing_in_it_once.
